<title>USA: Harmon Industries purchases facility.</title>
<headline>Harmon Industries purchases facility.</headline>
<dateline>BLUE SPRINGS, Mo. 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Harmon Industries Inc said Monday it purchased a facility and additional 15 acres in the Warrensburg Industrial Center, four miles east of the Harmon plants now located in Warrensburg, Mo.</p>
<p>Harmon said an existing building on the new property will be used immediately for assembly and wiring purposes. Ultimately this property, along with other Harmon facilities in Warrensburg, may be developed in a multi-facility, high-tech complex, it added.</p>
<p>Harmon employs about 300 people in Warrensburg. It expects to create 100 new jobs by the end of the year.</p>
<p>Harmon supplies signal and train control products to railroads and transit systems.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
